w/articleshow/135207740.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135207740.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/he-is-aged-can-say-such-things-tmc-mamata-faction-mp-defends-kharge-amid-baap-remark-row/articleshow/135207740.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/he-is-aged-can-say-such-things-tmc-mamata-faction-mp-defends-kharge-amid-baap-remark-row/articleshow/135207740.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-26T15:13:20+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Karan Manral</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135208263,imgsize-149692.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Unforgivable': MP minister Vishvas Sarang slams Kharge over remark on PM Modi]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/unforgivable-mp-minister-vishvas-sarang-slams-kharge-over-remark-on-pm-modi/articleshow/135206540.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135206540.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[In a recent event marking Dr. Krishna Singh's birth anniversary in Patna, Madhya Pradesh minister Vishvas Sarang took aim at Congress president Mallikarjun Kharge for his disparaging remarks about Prime Minister Narendra Modi's late parents. Sarang criticized the need for greater respect towards cultural customs surrounding the deceased, labeling Kharge's comments as wholly unacceptable. He condemned the Congress party's silence on the matter, voicing concern over their current political behavior.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/unforgivable-mp-minister-vishvas-sarang-slams-kharge-over-remark-on-pm-modi/articleshow/135206540.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/unforgivable-mp-minister-vishvas-sarang-slams-kharge-over-remark-on-pm-modi/articleshow/135206540.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-26T13:55:48+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Mahima Sharma</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135206861,imgsize-185087.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['We hear you': Rahul Gandhi's message to traders in Delhi amid anti-CEC stir]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/we-hear-you-rahul-gandhis-message-to-traders-in-delhi-amid-anti-cec-stir/articleshow/135206564.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135206564.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Rahul Gandhi has publicly backed the traders in Delhi struggling from the ramifications of ongoing protests and governmental restrictions. He pointed fingers at the administration for hampering commerce by suspending metro services and blocking roads. Traders are reportedly facing losses of around Rs 3,000 crore following previous rallies in October.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/we-hear-you-rahul-gandhis-message-to-traders-in-delhi-amid-anti-cec-stir/articleshow/135206564.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/we-hear-you-rahul-gandhis-message-to-traders-in-delhi-amid-anti-cec-stir/articleshow/135206564.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-26T13:51:24+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Trisha Mahajan</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135206803,imgsize-52906.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Australia expands biometric requirements for visa applicants in India from October 26]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/australia-expands-biometric-requirements-for-visa-applicants-in-india-